<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Embraer 1996 loss lower.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Embraer 1996 loss lower.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian aircraft manufacturer Embraer issued the following statement on its 1996 results.</p>
<p>			1996				 1995</p>
<p>    loss	   41.6 million		     318.8 million</p>
<p>    rvs	    431 million			376.5 million</p>
<p>NOTE: All data in Brazilian reais. No per share figures were provided.</p>
<p>The company said it managed to reduce its losses last year due to an ongoing restructuring plan to cut production and indirect costs and increase productivity and competitiveness.</p>
<p>Under this plan, Embraer cut its workforce and financial costs, found third parties to take over secondary activities not related to its main core business, invested in computerising and sealed contracts to sell its new 50-seat jet EMB-145, it said.</p>
<p>((--Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
